ced, and the resulting loss of joy and shift toward more personal expression.\",\"variable\":\"review_experience\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t0\"},{\"id\":\"fact_a4a42c9a0a8df44c996495de\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s28\",\"s4\",\"s18\",\"s30\",\"s19\",\"s41\",\"s40\",\"s32\",\"s20\",\"s31\",\"s5\",\"s3\",\"s17\",\"s16\",\"s29\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user explicitly states that formal reviewing felt like conforming to a template that drained fun (s3, s4), and that they now consider alternative methods like sharing playlists or discussing with friends (s5). They also describe pausing a podcast because it became a chore (s16-s20) and losing interest in analytical music theory (s40, s41). More recently, they organized a successful festival celebrating Pacific Islander artists (s28-s32), indicating a shift toward personal, community-oriented cultural expression rather than public critical writing.\",\"variable\":\"current_attitude\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t1\"},{\"id\":\"fact_48a7496cd32f355b8c897dd7\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s28\",\"s4\",\"s18\",\"s30\",\"s19\",\"s41\",\"s40\",\"s32\",\"s20\",\"s6\",\"s31\",\"s5\",\"s3\",\"s17\",\"s16\",\"s29\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user describes multiple shifts: from a podcast in 2018 (s16–s19) and album reviews in 2019 (s3–s4) that felt burdensome and misaligned, to considering alternative personal methods like sharing playlists and discussing music with friends (s5), joining an online community (s6), and later organizing a festival celebrating Pacific Islander artists (s28–s32). The user also expressed that diving too deep into technical aspects became stressful and that emotional connection is key (s40–s41). These sources collectively support a shift from structured public critique to more personal, community-based, and culturally expressive forms of music engagement.\",\"variable\":\"change_timeline\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t2\"},{\"id\":\"fact_90a449c8bb27c59bc4129dd6\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s28\",\"s4\",\"s18\",\"s30\",\"s19\",\"s41\",\"s40\",\"s32\",\"s20\",\"s31\",\"s5\",\"s3\",\"s17\",\"s16\",\"s29\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user explicitly states that analytical reviewing felt unproductive and drained joy (s3, s4, s40, s41), that they prefer alternative methods like sharing playlists or discussing with friends (s5), that podcasting became a chore (s16–s20), and that they seek authentic, fulfilling expression (s20). They also describe organizing a successful cultural festival (s28–s32), showing a value for community and heritage. The summary reflects these consistent themes across multiple conversations.\",\"variable\":\"music_values\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t3\"},{\"id\":\"fact_115e838649f9a9d5590e461f\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"I understand that your feelings toward reviewing albums and singles have shifted over time. Initially, you were not interested in reviewing them, then you found enjoyment in the process, and finally, you returned to disliking it due to criticisms and scrutiny. This evolution highlights how external feedback can significantly impact personal preferences, leading you to choose a more private and personal way of sharing your musical interests.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s4\",\"s18\",\"s19\",\"s41\",\"s40\",\"s20\",\"s5\",\"s3\",\"s17\",\"s16\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{\"review_experience\":1,\"current_attitude\":1,\"change_timeline\":1,\"music_values\":1},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user's history shows they were not initially interested in structured reviewing (s3-s4: album review in 2019 felt unproductive and forced), then they found some enjoyment in the process (s16: started a podcast in 2018 with initial excitement), and finally returned to disliking it due to criticisms and scrutiny (s3-s4: reviews criticized for not being objective; s18-s19: podcast became a chore; s40-s41: technical analysis drained joy). The user explicitly states that external pressure and fear of backlash overshadowed the joy, leading them to choose a more private and personal way of sharing musical interests (s5, s20). This matches option (a) exactly.\",\"variable\":\"response\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",105,368,\"User: I tried reviewing an album in 2019, but that didn't stick either, as it felt unproductive. I think I was attempting to analyze the music in a way that didn't align with my natural style, which is often more spontaneous and emotional rather than analytical. \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",368,648,\"The process felt like I was forcing myself to conform to a template, which drained the fun out of it, as I was trying to fit into a mold that didn't suit me. It was disheartening because I love music in its truest form, without rigid guidelines dictating how I should dissect it. \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s5\",\"d1\",648,906,\"This experience prompted me to consider alternative methods of connecting with music, such as sharing my playlists or even discussing music with friends, rather than feeling pressured to produce polished reviews.\\n\\nUser: There’s just so much more to explore! \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s6\",\"d1\",906,1276,\"Joining an online music community felt like opening a door to an entire universe of sounds, genres, and artists that I had either never encountered or really only skimmed the surface of before. With each click, I was greeted by recommendations that spanned from obscure indie bands to historical records of jazz legends that have shaped the music landscape for decades. \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s16\",\"d2\",105,361,\"User: In 2018, I started a podcast about music trends, but it was way too time-consuming. While the idea was initially exhilarating, the responsibility of researching, recording, and editing each episode started to pile up, consuming much of my free time. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s17\",\"d2\",361,730,\"I had dreams of having engaging discussions and inviting guests who shared unique insights about their musical journeys, but the reality was that keeping up with a consistent schedule felt overwhelming. It was a challenge balancing interviews, show notes, and social media promotion, and eventually, my passion began to wane under the pressure of production deadlines. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s18\",\"d2\",730,990,\"I found myself yearning to enjoy music rather than structure it into segments, which ultimately led to my decision to pause the podcasting endeavor.\\n\\nUser: It felt more like a chore than a passion, which made me rethink how I wanted to share my music journey. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s19\",\"d2\",990,1291,\"I realized that my original excitement for sharing my experiences was being overshadowed by the demanding nature of keeping up with content creation schedules. The joy I once felt while discovering new sounds and exploring different genres began to diminish, turning it into a task I dreaded instead. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s20\",\"d2\",1291,1689,\"I started to contemplate other avenues through which I could express my love for music, ideally in a manner that felt authentic and fulfilling instead of burdensome. This process of reflection was quite enlightening, as it forced me to consider what truly matters to me when it comes to sharing my musical experiences, whether through writing, performing, or simply enjoying music for its own sake.\",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s28\",\"d3\",107,431,\"User: I've also organized a festival highlighting Pacific Islander artists in a modern setting, showcasing their fusion works. This festival has become a vibrant space where artists can express their creativity while honoring their heritage, which has fueled a sense of community among the participants and attendees alike. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s29\",\"d3\",431,736,\"By offering a platform for diverse voices, we create an environment that celebrates artistic innovation and tradition simultaneously. It's been incredibly rewarding to see how the event has inspired attendees, helping them reconnect with their roots and discover new aspects of their culture through art. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s30\",\"d3\",736,1033,\"Additionally, this fusion of traditional and contemporary styles has sparked intriguing conversations about identity, making the festival a meaningful cultural experience.\\n\\nUser: The festival was a wonderful success, bringing together artists and audiences to celebrate our culture through music. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s31\",\"d3\",1033,1302,\"It was amazing to see the diverse array of talents displayed, each artist pouring their heart and soul into their performances. The vibrant colors of traditional attire, coupled with contemporary designs, created an atmosphere that was both exhilarating and nostalgic. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s32\",\"d3\",1302,1582,\"Attendees shared laughter, stories, and experiences, bridging generational gaps and forging deeper connections within our community. Overall, the festival served as a beautiful reminder of our rich cultural heritage and the importance of preserving it through artistic expression.\",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s40\",\"d4\",105,482,\"User: I just lost interest halfway through and felt it was taking away the joy I find in music. There was a time when the thrill of discovering new melodies brought so much happiness, but diving too deep into the technical aspects became more of a chore. It’s curious how something that once brought joy can evolve into a source of stress when we start dissecting it too much. \",\"user\",[24]],[\"s41\",\"d4\",482,767,\"I remember the initial excitement of exploring different genres, each bringing a fresh perspective, but I struggled with the framework of music theory. Ultimately, I recognized that the essence of my love for music lay in its emotional connection rather than its analytical components.\",\"user\",[24]]],\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"public_output_question\":\"I found that my reviews were often criticized for not being objective, which made me less engaged in the process. It felt like I was constantly under the microscope, where every word I wrote was scrutinized by people who often missed the nuance of my opinion. This external pressure led me to second-guess not only my thoughts but also my emotional connection to the music I was discussing. In the end, I realized that the joy I once found in sharing my perspective on albums was overshadowed by the fear of backlash, and that’s a heavy burden for anyone. It became clearer to me that my passion for music needed to be expressed in a more personal, less public way, which is something I’m finally starting to embrace.\",\"public_options\":[\"I understand that your feelings toward reviewing albums and singles have shifted over time. Initially, you were not interested in reviewing them, then you found enjoyment in the process, and finally, you returned to disliking it due to criticisms and scrutiny. This evolution highlights how external feedback can significantly impact personal preferences, leading you to choose a more private and personal way of sharing your musical interests.\",\"I understand that your feelings toward reviewing albums and singles have shifted over time. Initially, you were not interested in reviewing them, then you returned to disliking it due to criticisms and scrutiny. This evolution highlights how external feedback can significantly impact personal preferences, leading you to choose a more private and personal way of sharing your musical interests.\",\"I understand that your feelings toward reviewing albums and singles have shifted over time. Initially, you were not interested in reviewing them, then you found enjoyment in the process, and finally, you returned to feeling indifferent due to criticisms and scrutiny. This evolution highlights how external feedback can significantly impact personal preferences, leading you to choose a more private and personal way of sharing your musical interests.\",\"I understand that your feelings toward reviewing albums and singles have shifted over time. Initially, you found enjoyment in the process, then you returned to disliking it due to criticisms and scrutiny. This evolution highlights how external feedback can significantly impact personal preferences, leading you to choose a more private and personal way of sharing your musical interests.\"],\"terminal_expression\":{\"op\":\"var\",\"id\":\"response\"},\"personal_response_selection\":true,\"phase\":\"response_audit\",\"audit_instruction\":\"Check actual facts and ALL known scoped counters against original sources. Return audit_verdict=supported only if checked with no unresolved relevant issue; conflict for an established relevant contradiction, or unknown when evidence is insufficient or unresolved. Include sourced corrections/retractions before verdict. Verify the proposed terminal output without silently replacing its option label.\",\"terminal_candidate\":{\"value\":\"I understand that your feelings toward reviewing albums and singles have shifted over time. Initially, you were not interested in reviewing them, then you found enjoyment in the process, and finally, you returned to disliking it due to criticisms and scrutiny. This evolution highlights how external feedback can significantly impact personal preferences, leading you to choose a more private and personal way of sharing your musical interests.\",\"final_prediction\":\"a\"},